    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-2,1)$ and $(0,-3)$.",
      "worked": "A vertical normal has a horizontal tangent, so $y'=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=3x^2+6x\\\\y'&=3x(x+2)\\\\0&=3x(x+2)\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }0\\\\y(-2)&=(-2)^3+3(-2)^2-3=1\\\\y(0)&=-3\\end{align*}$$\nThe points are $(-2,1)$ and $(0,-3)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
